It is so incredibly overrated, that I am wondering if something fishy is going on with the User Reviews. This movie isn't completely shit, don't get me wrong, but it is a 6 at most, if you are a Tom Cruise fan and are easily entertained/have half a brain cell. Here's a list of reasons why (no spoilers):

1) The plot of this movie is so unoriginal: the stuck-in-a-time-loop cliché is combined with the SciFi element of alien invasion (which is also nothing new);

2) They don't even give an explanation for the invasion apart from "the aliens want to conquer the world";

3) Apparently the entire military consists only of footsoldiers and a few heli's or planes;

4) A "super weapon" that is supposed to make humans more on par with the obviously superior aliens is nothing more than a clunky, slow, metal suit that can shoot a gun. This, apparently, is supposed to be much better than a usual soldier with a gun. Fine, let's just accept it as a valid weapon, but a super weapon to fight a global alien invasion and this is the best you can come up with? "I pew pew from my suit instead of from the gun, suck it, aliens!"

5) The stuck-in-a-time loop "rules" so to speak are about as consistent/stable as a teenagers mood swings (I won't give examples to avoid spoilers but they are in just about every scene);

6) The side-characters are so incredibly flat that you as a viewer don't give a darn about them and they aren't even funny to compensate entertainment-wise;

7) One of my main grievances: the character design of the aliens is sooo uninspired, it is incredibly disappointing. If you make a movie about aliens, MAKE THE ALIENS COOL PLEASE. Isn't that at least half of what we watch such movies for??

8) The aliens move so fast and chaotically (, or at least they are CG animated as such) that the first half of the movie I literally got annoyed that I just wanted to get ONE good look at them. Just one... Later you get a chance to actually get a better look, but as mentioned, their design is sadly boring.

9) Another point with the aliens moving fast and having all kinds of overpowered skills is how incredibly unlikely it is that mankind actually stands the slightest chance to even put up a fight. It's basically level snowman vs sahara sun and you as the viewer are expected on how the snowman won't melt out of sheer willpower;

10) The main character is a cowardly whimp in the beginning of the movie and through the time-loop repetition he becomes more couragious each (same) day. Still, such extraordinary personality changes take way more time and you don't become a professional warrior be repeating the same day. Soldiers take longer than a few months in their training, so following that logic, the short time the main character repeats the same day and goes from zero to hero is silly. If this argument doesn't convince you, there is also an optional 11) --> It is said in the movie only the same day is repeated, but many of the travels, events and actions just have to take up more than a day's time, so what happened to 'one day only'?

All in all, the acting isn't great (though not terrible, it seems pretty lackluster apart from really solid action acting) and it is not enough to make up for all of the parts of this movie that make me feel like I'm a dumbass for even watching it. It was entertaining, so I feel it is a missed opportunity to be a good movie, but as states above: the story is unoriginal and has more holes in the plot than there are holes in fishnet stocking. Thanks for reading the rant, I'm off to watch what cinemasins has to say about this movie ;)
